This paper determines the asymptotic behavior of recurrence coefficients for polynomials orthogonal against the logarithmic weight $w(x,t)=\log t$ on the interval $[0,1]$, where $t=x^{\alpha}$ and $\alpha>0$. Our findings complement a recent theorem by Rakhmanov, which establishes the specific case where $\alpha=1$. Furthermore, we derive a stronger version of Szegő's theorem and a novel asymptotic formula for the value of the $n$-th orthogonal polynomial at $x=1$. These results are supported by a new method for constructing the matrix of recurrence coefficients, an approach that is also applicable to other measures. Specifically, we demonstrate that the recurrence coefficients $(\beta_n)_{n\geq 0}$ and $(\gamma_n)_{n\geq 1}$ associated with the orthogonal polynomials $(p_n)_{n\geq 0}$ satisfy the following asymptotic relations:
\begin{align*}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\beta_n&=1,\quad \lim_{n\to\infty}n(1-\beta_n)=\frac{\alpha}{2},
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align*}
\lim_{n\to\infty}n^2\left(\gamma_n-{\frac{1}{4n^2}}\right)&=-\frac{\alpha(\alpha-1)}{8}.
\end{align*}
